  "observations": [
    "Final native provider suite passes 200 checks/26 complete images; shared wire suite 391/26; unchanged compiled previous list client 140/26. Both browser list suites and Chromium overflowing-list suite pass with the unchanged adapters; button/text regressions pass against the same shared SDK. Scoped totals derive from the listed final result files. All 35 existing UI/provider/transport sections pass separately.",
    "Grid tests compare actual GNUstep view and cell decisions with independent ordinary windows rather than reconstructing them from row rectangles. Queries preserve native state/focus and can read during native tracking. Full uint64 IDs cross IPC without double conversion.",
    "Actual previous providers reject the optional API/IPC query without writing the caller buffer. Existing list/scroll capability values remain stable. Creating-connection checks reject foreign item metadata reads.",
    "Separate loader and provider source reproductions are byte-identical. Original production components, previous SDKs and browser adapters retain hashes. Real renderer sandboxing is measured by fixture ancestry. All owned fixtures stop and no owned candidate mappings remain.",
    "Build and orchestration errors are retained separately: an incorrect GCC Objective-C include override, a stream socket used for a SEQPACKET fixture, a nonexistent Chromium test filename, readiness checks before the launch record/window existed, and a Firefox test port that differed from its launcher. None is counted as a passing product suite."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Bind native item IDs into original browser hit-result/event targets with native root/non-item behavior, stable identity revalidation, original trusted dispatch, cancellation, hover/enter/leave/related-target semantics and default focus.",
    "Complete Firefox list viewport/native row geometry and scrolling using the shared measurements/transport, then qualify the required native target checks in both engines.",
    "Full option/intrinsic layout contracts, held-scroller DOM synchronization, richer models/CSS/transforms/zoom/scales, host recovery, IME/accessibility, other browser builds/derivatives and installed deployment.",
    "Remaining webpage controls, detached menus and native shortcuts, then GTK/Qt/KDE using the shared UI library and bridge. Optional future toolbar/UI changes belong in app-specific patches; current toolbar/address bar/tabs remain original."
  ],
  "source_audit": "item-hit-source-audit.json"
